<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36856" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pollentĭa</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pōlent-</span></b> ),
			ae, f.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A city in Picenum</i>, now <i>Monte
				Moline</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Phil. 11, 6, 14</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Fam.
				11, 13, 3</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pollentīni</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., <i>the Pollentians</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 13, 18, §
			111</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A city in Liguria</i>, now <i>Pollenza</i>, <i><span class="en">Col. 7, 2, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 14,
				157</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sil. 8, 598</span></i>.—Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pollentī-nus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pōlent-</span></b> ),
				a, um, adj., <i>of</i>
			or <i>belonging to Pollentia</i>, <i>Pollentian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">plebs,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Tib. 37</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
